p.src:
Write an abstract vector in Dirac notation as $\ket{\alpha}$. A concrete representation is $\ket{\alpha}
  \longleftrightarrow
  \begin{pmatrix}
    \alpha_1\\
    \alpha_2
  \end{pmatrix},
  \qquad
  \alpha_1,\alpha_2\in\mathbb C.$ If $\ket{\beta}
  \longleftrightarrow
  \begin{pmatrix}
    \beta_1\\
    \beta_2
  \end{pmatrix},$ then addition and scalar multiplication are defined component by component: $\begin{aligned}\ket{\alpha}+\ket{\beta}
  &\longleftrightarrow
  \begin{pmatrix}
    \alpha_1+\beta_1\\
    \alpha_2+\beta_2
  \end{pmatrix},\\
  z\ket{\alpha}
  &\longleftrightarrow
  \begin{pmatrix}
    z\alpha_1\\
    z\alpha_2
  \end{pmatrix},
  \qquad z\in\mathbb C.\end{aligned}$

